# The build context is the repo root. Allowlist, not blocklist: exclude
# everything, then admit only what the build reads, so a database dump or a
# Chrome profile dropped in the tree never gets uploaded to the daemon.

*

# --- what the build actually reads ------------------------------------------
!cmd/
!UI/
!local-infra/db/

# ...and, for `./build.sh --images`, the finished executables the packaging
# Dockerfiles wrap. Named file by file, not `!bin/`: a `global` written next to
# a binary on a server checkout must never ride along into the context.
!bin/ubuntu/huntwell
!bin/ubuntu/website
!bin/ubuntu/admin
!bin/ubuntu/planning
!bin/ubuntu/worker
!bin/ubuntu/scheduling
!bin/ubuntu/notification
!bin/ubuntu-arm64/huntwell
!bin/ubuntu-arm64/website
!bin/ubuntu-arm64/admin
!bin/ubuntu-arm64/planning
!bin/ubuntu-arm64/worker
!bin/ubuntu-arm64/scheduling
!bin/ubuntu-arm64/notification

# --- and what to leave behind inside those ----------------------------------
cmd/target/
**/node_modules/
UI/*/dist/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
